    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this decides the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-03201. What the record shows. The driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 17:23:46; the free waiting period in force was 180 s (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec); the wait timer started at 17:23:48; the driver cancelled at 17:30:38 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. The GPS trace records a single unbroken in-geofence run of 410 s (42 fixes), and the rider's own device sits 599-606 m from the pickup pin throughout the window, so the rider was not at the pickup point and the driver's account of a rider who did not appear is consistent with the trace. Why the fee is refunded in full (SGD 4.50). POL-NS-01 charges a no-show fee only if all four of its limbs hold, and limb (b) requires the gps_trace to place the driver inside the pickup geofence on the terms of POL-NS-02. That clause deems the driver arrived only where the trace contains at least three consecutive fixes 'each with reported horizontal accuracy of 25 m or better' within the arrival radius (50 m for this STANDARD pickup). EV-GPS-03201 reports no horizontal accuracy for any of its fixes: its payload carries fix counts, distances and speeds, and its derived block carries no accuracy value at all; the '42 qualifying fixes' and the 410 s run rest on distance and dwell alone. POL-NS-12, which lets platform telemetry stand in for a sparse or accuracy-less export, does not apply: it operates only where platform_policy.arrival_marker is GPS_AUTO and the platform's arrival event states its own geofence test, and this record's marker is BUTTON ('Driver tapped I'm Here'), which POL-NS-12 says in terms is not covered. Limb (b) is therefore not established on this record, the closing sentence of POL-NS-02 follows, and the cancellation fee is refunded in full; no driver compensation is payable. Claims addressed. Driver's claims 1-4 (arrival inside the 50 m radius, the 410 s dwell against the 180 s minimum, termination under RIDER_NO_SHOW after the dwell, and the marker not being false under POL-NS-05) are accepted as far as they go - the marker is genuine and the dwell is real - but proximity, dwell and a genuine marker do not supply the accuracy POL-NS-02 requires, so they do not make limb (b) out. Driver's claim 5 (no POL-NS-08 impairment) is accepted: there is no clock skew, no trace gap, no chat defect and no fare mismatch; a missing accuracy figure is not an impairment under POL-NS-08(a)-(d), so it neither escalates the case nor lifts the clause's own test. Driver's claims 6-7 (POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider, POL-NS-03 does not apply) are accepted and are immaterial, because the fee fails on the driver's own limb (b). Driver's claims 8-9 (the chat log shows the driver coordinating from the pin, and the rider's 'only a few minutes late' account is contradicted by her track 600 m away) are accepted as facts but do not cure limb (b); the driver's counterparty statement is likewise noted but no clause of this category names a counterparty statement as the test for arrival. Driver's claims 10-11 (POL-NS-07 payout of 80% of 4.50 = SGD 3.60, anti-farming clear, and a DRIVER_COMPENSATION disposition) are rejected in their outcome: the arithmetic is right and the anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 0 against 95 completed trips in 30 days), but compensation only arises where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not. Rider's claims 1-2 (POL-NS-04 limbs (a) and (b) are made out but limb (c) is not) are accepted; POL-NS-04 therefore exonerates no one, and this is immaterial to the outcome. Rider's claim 3 is accepted and decides the case for the reasons above. Discarded claim: the driver's claim about the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-03201-01 was discarded by the referee because it cited a zero-weight artifact (MISSING_ARTIFACT) without naming its issue code, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires; it is not relied on here. The monetary effect, a SGD 4.50 refund, does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold. Confidence is 0.85: the ruling rests on EV-GPS-03201 and EV-TRIP-03201, each at full weight 1.0, and no relied-on artifact sits below the 0.70 floor."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-03201-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 and no payload — no advisory covers this pickup in this window — so the accumulation limb POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable; that costs the driver nothing here, because his dwell is one uninterrupted 410-second run at a single in-geofence position (run_count 1) that already exceeds the minimum without summing any second interval. The absence of an advisory is disclosed, and the impairment is immaterial to this claim.",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-03201-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "side": "DRIVER"
    }
  ]
}
